@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-s2-average-wage-and-schedule-a`

-- TESTS for s 2 and Schedule A (row IL-34). Expected values worked by hand from the Hebrew; the arithmetic is beside each group.
-- The measured wages are round ILLUSTRATIVE figures (the CBS's series is an input and not deposited).

§ `Tests: section 2 and Schedule A`

§§ `Fixtures: compensation`

`no compensation` MEANS `The compensation that applied in a month` WITH `its rate` IS 0, `its amount in shekels` IS 0
`a compensation of 2% or 150 shekels` MEANS `The compensation that applied in a month` WITH `its rate` IS 0.02, `its amount in shekels` IS 150
`a compensation of 1% or 100 shekels` MEANS `The compensation that applied in a month` WITH `its rate` IS 0.01, `its amount in shekels` IS 100
`a large compensation that must not be used` MEANS `The compensation that applied in a month` WITH `its rate` IS 0.5, `its amount in shekels` IS 9_999

§§ `Section 2(a): the exceptional wage month`

#ASSERT     `s 2(a) — month` 12 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 2(a) — month` 11 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 2(a) — month` 7 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE
#ASSERT     `s 2(a) — month` 7 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 2(a) — month` 12 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(a) — month` 0 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` TRUE BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(a) — month` 13 `is an exceptional wage month, allowances to most employees being` FALSE BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"

§§ `Section 2(a): the corrected measured wage`

-- The last month before the exceptional month measured 12,000; no compensation: 12,000 + 0.5% x 12,000 = 12,060 (no reading consulted).
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` FALSE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `no compensation` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `no compensation` EQUALS 12_060
-- With compensation of 2% (or 150): 12,060 + 12,000 x 0.02 = 12,300 as a rate; 12,060 + 150 = 12,210 as an amount; declined by default.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` FALSE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a compensation of 2% or 150 shekels` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `no compensation` `, reading it as` `the compensation is added as its rate of the earlier month's measured wage` EQUALS 12_300
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` FALSE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a compensation of 2% or 150 shekels` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `no compensation` `, reading it as` `the compensation is added as its amount in shekels` EQUALS 12_210
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` FALSE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a compensation of 2% or 150 shekels` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `no compensation` BECAUSE "section 2(a) adds \"compensation\" and does not say whether as a rate of the earlier month's measured wage or as an amount in shekels"
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the reading this row takes of the compensation added` EQUALS `how the compensation is added is declined`
-- The last month before was itself exceptional: the month before IT (11,000) is used, with the compensation of THE EARLIER month:
-- 11,000 + 55 = 11,055; plus 1% x 11,000 = 110 as a rate (11,165) or 100 as an amount (11,155). The later month's large compensation is not used.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` TRUE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a large compensation that must not be used` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `a compensation of 1% or 100 shekels` `, reading it as` `the compensation is added as its rate of the earlier month's measured wage` EQUALS 11_165
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` TRUE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a large compensation that must not be used` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `a compensation of 1% or 100 shekels` `, reading it as` `the compensation is added as its amount in shekels` EQUALS 11_155
-- ... and with no compensation in the earlier month the large one never matters: 11,055, at the default.
#ASSERT `s 2(a) — the corrected measured wage: the month before measured` 12_000 `, that month being exceptional:` TRUE `, the month before it measured` 11_000 `, compensation then` `a large compensation that must not be used` `and in the earlier exceptional month` `no compensation` EQUALS 11_055

§§ `Section 2(b)(2): the monthly difference and the increase`

-- (13,200 - 12,000) / 12,000 = 0.1; equal wages 0; (11,400 - 12,000) / 12,000 = -0.05.
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` 13_200 `and corrected` 12_000 EQUALS 0.1
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` 12_000 `and corrected` 12_000 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` 11_400 `and corrected` 12_000 EQUALS -0.05
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(b)(2) — the monthly difference: measured` 100 `and corrected` 0 BECAUSE "a monthly difference is divided by the corrected measured wage, which is 0"
-- 13,000 x (1 + (0.1 + 0.01 + 0.01) / 12) = 13,000 x 1.01 = 13,130; two known months, the same sum: 13,130; none: 13,000; four: refused.
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` 13_000 `with the monthly differences` (LIST 0.1, 0.01, 0.01) EQUALS 13_130
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` 13_000 `with the monthly differences` (LIST 0.11, 0.01) EQUALS 13_130
#ASSERT `s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` 13_000 `with the monthly differences` (EMPTY) EQUALS 13_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 2(b)(2) — the average wage increased: computed` 13_000 `with the monthly differences` (LIST 0.1, 0.01, 0.01, 0.01) BECAUSE "section 2(b)(2) takes the last three exceptional wage months, and more than three monthly differences were given"

§§ `Schedule A: 15% of the average wage on the first day of the quarter`

-- 15% x 13,566 (the average wage under s 1 from 1 January 2026, as the consolidation's note prints it) = 2,034.9, for each month of the first quarter.
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 1 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 2_034.9
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 3 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 EQUALS 2_034.9
-- A later quarter with a different average wage (illustrative 14,000): 15% x 14,000 = 2,100.
#ASSERT `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 4 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 14_000 EQUALS 2_100
#ASSERT REFUSED `Schedule A — the minimum average monthly income for month` 0 `, the average wage on the first day of the quarter's first month being` 13_566 BECAUSE "a month of the tax year is numbered from 1 to 12"
